Third-Party Notices
===================

Kept out of LICENSE so that GitHub and other licence scanners can detect the
MIT licence. A LICENSE file with anything appended after the MIT text is
reported as NOASSERTION, which reads as "unlicensed" to tooling.

CheckLink's own code is Stormberry AS's and is published in this repository
under the MIT licence. Since stage 2 (11 October 2026) it also ships
third-party code and data, listed below: a QR and barcode decoder, the Public
Suffix List and the word lists of wallet recovery phrases (BIP-39, Monero
and SLIP-39), plus one typeface. Stage 3 (11 October 2026) added Unicode's
look-alike character data, and stage 4b (the same day) a QR code encoder.
Everything in the web app is
vendored: copied into this repository at an exact version, never loaded from
a content delivery network, and nothing is downloaded at build or run time.
The Android app (android/, stage 4) is the one exception, at build time
only: see its section below. tools/upstream.lock.json records, for every
web item, the exact version or
commit, the source address, its size, its sha256 (and for the npm package its
sha512 integrity as the registry publishes it) and its licence, and
`node tools/vendor.mjs --check` proves the files here still match it.

NOTICE is not published with the site or the app, so the licence texts also
ship in licences/, which is.

